1
00:01:23,441 --> 00:01:27,108
اَعُوْذُ بِاللهِ مِنَّ الشِّيْطَانِ الرَّجِيْمِ۝ بِسْمِ اللهِ الرَّحْمَانِ الرَّحِيْمَ۝

2
00:01:28,155 --> 00:01:33,548
اَلْحَمْدُ لله ، وَالصَّلَاةُ وَالسَّلَامُ عَلى سَيِّدِنَا محمد وَعَلَى اَلِهِ وَصَحْبِهِ وَسَلِّمْ تَسْلِيْمًا كَثِيْراً

3
00:01:33,982 --> 00:01:35,457
اَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكُمْ وَرَحْمَةُ الله

4
00:01:40,780 --> 00:01:48,396
Tonight In sha'Allah Ta'ala(إن شاء الله تعالى) we'll move on to the second half of the conquests

5
00:01:50,339 --> 00:01:56,004
and that's the Roman front, remember they were dealing with two fronts.

6
00:01:56,710 --> 00:02:05,980
The Persian Empire in Al-Iraq and then the Roman Empire in the land of Ash-Sham(ألشام)

7
00:02:07,931 --> 00:02:12,447
and this is called Ghazwa Ur Rome(غزوة ألروم), the conquest of Ar-Rome(ألروم).

8
00:02:13,025 --> 00:02:19,013
Now, sometimes there could be confusion in what is meant by Ar-Rome(ألروم).

9
00:02:20,965 --> 00:02:27,670
Ar-Rome(ألروم) in Arabic is a name designated to an ethnic group, it is not a land,

10
00:02:30,580 --> 00:02:40,535
 it is an ethnic group and that is what we call today the Caucasian or the European or the white people.

11
00:02:41,148 --> 00:02:43,048
In Arabic, they are called Ar-Rome(ألروم).

12
00:02:44,181 --> 00:02:46,563
So, whenever you hear Hadith(حديث) about Ar-Rome(ألروم),

13
00:02:47,368 --> 00:02:52,583
it's not really talking about the political entity, the Roman Empire, per se.

14
00:02:52,806 --> 00:02:55,417
But it was talking about a people,

15
00:02:56,377 --> 00:03:00,572
 regardless of where they were living, because Ash-sham(ألشام) was not part of Europe.

16
00:03:01,759 --> 00:03:10,933
As-Sham(ألشام) Syria, Phalastine(فلسطين), Jordan and Lebanon, but it was ruled by the Romans.

17
00:03:12,965 --> 00:03:14,918
In those days, there were two Roman Empire's.

18
00:03:14,943 --> 00:03:17,685
The Eastern Roman Empire and The Western Roman Empire.

19
00:03:17,710 --> 00:03:23,340
The Eastern one, was called the Byzantine Empire - Al-Emaraturiya Al-Bayzantia(ألإماراتيه ألّبزانتيه).

20
00:03:26,210 --> 00:03:34,803
So, Ar-Rome(ألروم) are the Caucasian people which are not the only living in Europe

21
00:03:34,827 --> 00:03:41,002
but they were living in those days in Russia, in Siberia

22
00:03:42,231 --> 00:03:45,684
and today in America and Australia, New Zealand.

23
00:03:46,701 --> 00:03:49,934
So, Ar-Rome(ألروم) or an ethnic people.

24
00:03:52,783 --> 00:03:59,151
The Ahadith(احاديث) of Fittan(فتن), of the end of time say that

25
00:04:00,221 --> 00:04:02,397
many of the Romans will become Muslim

26
00:04:03,954 --> 00:04:11,662
but however, the leadership of the camp that will be fighting against the Muslims,

27
00:04:12,501 --> 00:04:14,388
will be in the hands of the Romans.

28
00:04:15,259 --> 00:04:23,526
So, for example, the most important war of the future which Rasool Allah ﷺ called Al-Malhama(ألملحمه),

29
00:04:23,910 --> 00:04:26,970
occurs between the Muslims and the Romans.

30
00:04:28,749 --> 00:04:32,661
And in that Hadith(حديث), it says that many of them became Muslim,

31
00:04:32,686 --> 00:04:38,109
because Romans will come to the Muslims and say, hand over the prisoners that you have taken away from us.

32
00:04:38,158 --> 00:04:41,273
So, the Muslims will say, No, we will never hand over our brothers.

33
00:04:42,893 --> 00:04:50,288
So, this also shows that the Muslims are not fighting a nationalistic war.

34
00:04:50,827 --> 00:04:57,503
It's not a war between Arabs and non Arabs, or Asians against Europeans that's not how it is.

35
00:04:58,519 --> 00:05:01,855
Because the Muslims said: These are our brothers,

36
00:05:02,610 --> 00:05:06,361
even though ethnically they are Roman, but because they are Muslim,

37
00:05:07,517 --> 00:05:10,224
they are our brothers, and we will never hand them over.

38
00:05:16,082 --> 00:05:20,651
Abu Bakr Siddique رضي الله عنه is the one, who opened this new front.

39
00:05:23,548 --> 00:05:33,182
And the Muslims fought the battle of Yarmook(يرموك), which was a major turning point battle, in Ash-Sham(ألشام).

40
00:05:33,752 --> 00:05:35,952
Al-Yarmook(أليرموك) is in present day Jordan.

41
00:05:38,517 --> 00:05:42,964
The Battle of Yarmook(أليرموك) itself, the preparation was done by Abu Bakr(ابوبكر),

42
00:05:42,988 --> 00:05:45,266
but he passed away before the actual battle.

43
00:05:45,533 --> 00:05:50,238
So, it happened in the rein of Umar Ibn Al-Khattab رضي الله عنه,

44
00:05:50,262 --> 00:05:55,576
but it was Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) who set the grounds for it.

45
00:05:58,246 --> 00:06:01,982
The next important event that happens in the time of Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب),

46
00:06:02,007 --> 00:06:04,385
was the siege of Damascus.

47
00:06:05,922 --> 00:06:10,942
Damascus was a very important town very well protected,

48
00:06:11,124 --> 00:06:17,654
it was surrounded by a wall which was built by the Romans, very well defended.

49
00:06:18,258 --> 00:06:22,604
So, it was a key town in Ash-Sham(ألشام).

50
00:06:24,452 --> 00:06:35,802
Umar Bin Khattab رضي الله عنه sent commands to his field commanders in Ash-Sham(ألشام) to the besiege Damascus

51
00:06:36,349 --> 00:06:40,722
 and focus on it rather than focus on opening other different towns

52
00:06:41,290 --> 00:06:42,562
for example, like HIMS(حمص).

53
00:06:43,796 --> 00:06:45,963
So, the Muslims laid siege to Damascus.

54
00:06:45,987 --> 00:06:49,835
Now, the weather in Syria is colder than the Arabian Peninsula.

55
00:06:50,433 --> 00:06:54,426
So, the weather is colder than what the Arabs are used to.

56
00:06:56,021 --> 00:07:01,855
So, the Romans were counting on winter to defeat the Muslim army

57
00:07:02,183 --> 00:07:03,463
but that didn't happened.

58
00:07:04,318 --> 00:07:09,486
In fact, it was said that the Roman soldiers would be well protected, wearing boots,

59
00:07:10,217 --> 00:07:14,498
while the Sahabah رضي الله عنهم were wearing sandals.

60
00:07:15,524 --> 00:07:18,313
Nevertheless, they survived for that entire winter.

61
00:07:22,547 --> 00:07:32,053
The Roman general or, a governor of Damascus had a newborn child.

62
00:07:33,036 --> 00:07:40,014
So, he held a Valeema(وليمه), an invitation, a party to celebrate.

63
00:07:42,578 --> 00:07:49,761
So, they had this feast and they got drunk.

64
00:07:51,535 --> 00:07:53,935
So, while they were drinking and partying,

65
00:07:54,684 --> 00:07:57,768
the intelligence of Khalid Ibn Walid(خالد ابن وليد),

66
00:07:57,833 --> 00:08:00,399
see the commander was Abu Obaidah(ابوعبيدة)

67
00:08:01,233 --> 00:08:04,038
and Abu Obaidah(ابوعبيدة) appointed under him, Khalid Ibn Walid(خالد ابن وليد),

68
00:08:04,413 --> 00:08:06,975
and Yazeed Ibn Abi Sufian(يزيدبن أبي سفيان), Sharhabeel Bin Hasana(شرهبيل بن حسنة)

69
00:08:07,232 --> 00:08:08,400
and Amr Bin Al-Aas(عَمْرُو بِن اَلْعَاص).

70
00:08:09,874 --> 00:08:13,502
And he appointed to them different gates to the city

71
00:08:13,625 --> 00:08:15,688
because the city of the Damascus had more than one gate.

72
00:08:16,665 --> 00:08:19,187
So, they were guarding each of these gates..

73
00:08:20,657 --> 00:08:27,742
 Khalid Ibn Walid(خالد ابن وليد) received intelligence of this party that the Roman governor was having.

74
00:08:28,248 --> 00:08:30,915
So, while they were busy drinking,

75
00:08:31,019 --> 00:08:35,027
Khalid Ibn Walid(خالد ابن وليد) and his men were busy installing ladders on the wall.

76
00:08:37,699 --> 00:08:39,652
And they had these hooked ropes

77
00:08:39,677 --> 00:08:42,642
that they would throw on top of the wall, and they would climb.

78
00:08:44,941 --> 00:08:50,785
Khalid Ibn Waleed رضي الله عنه and a few of the Sahabah(صحابه),

79
00:08:51,881 --> 00:08:54,023
such as Al-Miqdar Ibn Amr(ألمقداد إبن عمرو) and others.

80
00:08:54,509 --> 00:08:57,101
They climbed the wall, it was a small group.

81
00:08:57,792 --> 00:09:00,959
They climbed the wall sneaked into town,

82
00:09:01,272 --> 00:09:02,756
and they started making Takbeer(تكبير),

83
00:09:03,936 --> 00:09:06,543
and remember that they had Miqdad Ibn Amr(ألمقداد إبن عمرو) with them.

84
00:09:07,999 --> 00:09:10,905
He was one whose voice is worth a 1000 men.

85
00:09:11,576 --> 00:09:13,867
So, his Takbeer(تكبير) was shaking Damascus,

86
00:09:18,145 --> 00:09:20,217
they took the Romans by surprise.

87
00:09:21,367 --> 00:09:30,084
So, the Roman governor rushed towards Abu Obaidah(ابوعبيدة), he just came out of Damascus

88
00:09:30,109 --> 00:09:31,898
and went to Abu Obaidah(ابوعبيدة) and said;

89
00:09:31,923 --> 00:09:34,785
We're ready to sign a peace agreement.

90
00:09:36,633 --> 00:09:41,769
They were offered, Al-Jizya(ألجزية) but they refused.

91
00:09:42,085 --> 00:09:46,686
Now, he just went and told Abu Obaidah(ابوعبيدة) I'm ready to sign the agreement, we'll pay Jizya(ألجزية).

92
00:09:47,616 --> 00:09:48,783
Abu Obaidah(ابوعبيدة) agreed

93
00:09:48,910 --> 00:09:51,933
because Abu Obaidah(ابوعبيدة) did not know what was happening in Damascus.

94
00:09:52,592 --> 00:09:55,416
He didn't know that Khalid Ibn Walid(خالد ابن وليد) and his men were already there.

95
00:09:56,077 --> 00:10:00,490
So, while Khalid Ibn Walid(خالد ابن وليد) and his men were fighting from one neighborhood to another,

96
00:10:00,697 --> 00:10:08,438
 taken over the town, Abu Obaidah(ابوعبيدة) was signing an agreement of surrender, with the Roman general.

97
00:10:10,912 --> 00:10:13,416
Later on, when they discovered what happened.

98
00:10:14,771 --> 00:10:17,781
Khalid Ibn Walid(خالد ابن وليد) has already taken over half of the town.

99
00:10:18,983 --> 00:10:20,392
So, what they did was,

100
00:10:21,217 --> 00:10:22,923
They came to an agreement

101
00:10:23,313 --> 00:10:31,295
that we will consider Damascus to be a town that half of it fell by occupation

102
00:10:31,320 --> 00:10:35,558
and the other half was through a peace agreement.

103
00:10:36,248 --> 00:10:45,886
And that's why the Muslims took half of the town including half of the Cathedral of Damascus.

104
00:10:45,984 --> 00:10:47,969
This was a great huge Cathedral.

105
00:10:48,437 --> 00:10:52,421
So, they decided that they're going to split everything in half including the cathedral.

106
00:10:52,843 --> 00:10:56,077
So, half of the cathedral was turned into a Masjid(مسجد)

107
00:10:56,371 --> 00:10:58,368
and the other half remained the cathedral.

108
00:11:00,223 --> 00:11:07,164
Later on, the Muslims purchased the other half and it became Al-Masjid Al Jamia(ألمسجدألجامع),

109
00:11:07,765 --> 00:11:09,805
which we call today Al-Masjid Al Ummvi(ألمسجدألأموي)

110
00:11:10,765 --> 00:11:14,345
and this is the main Masjid(مسجد) in the city of Dimashq(دمشق).

111
00:11:17,453 --> 00:11:23,505
Because what falls by force, everything is taken over by the army,

112
00:11:23,530 --> 00:11:26,546
however when you sign an agreement that they pay the Jizya(ألجزية),

113
00:11:26,851 --> 00:11:29,847
they protect their property and blood is protected.

114
00:11:33,836 --> 00:11:37,712
But as they say Khalid Ibn Walid(خالد ابن وليد) would not sleep

115
00:11:37,737 --> 00:11:40,845
and he would not give anybody the privilege of sleeping,

116
00:11:41,111 --> 00:11:43,257
he would not allow anybody the privilege of sleeping.

117
00:11:43,869 --> 00:11:47,502
So, while there were celebrating he was awake and busy.

118
00:11:50,147 --> 00:12:00,084
In fact, Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) when he sent orders to As-Sham(ألشام) to send back an army to Iraq.

119
00:12:00,678 --> 00:12:01,462
 He said;

120
00:12:02,501 --> 00:12:06,013
You see, in the beginning there was an army in Iraq led by Khalid Ibn Walid(خالد ابن وليد).

121
00:12:07,626 --> 00:12:09,967
Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) told him to go to Syria.

122
00:12:10,800 --> 00:12:12,987
So, Khalid Ibn Walid(خالد ابن وليد) and his army went to Syria.

123
00:12:14,245 --> 00:12:15,885
When things were changing in Al-Iraq,

124
00:12:16,222 --> 00:12:18,331
Al Qadsiyya(ألقادسية), and An-Nahwand(ألنهوند) major battles.

125
00:12:18,596 --> 00:12:22,994
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) told Abu Obaidah(ابوعبيدة) to send the army of Iraq back to Iraq

126
00:12:23,994 --> 00:12:29,844
 but he said: Send them back however, keep with you Khalid Ibn Walid(خالد ابن وليد)

127
00:12:30,320 --> 00:12:31,288
because you would need him.

128
00:12:32,757 --> 00:12:38,786
So, Abu Obaidah kept Khalid Ibn Walid(خالد ابن وليد) with him  in Damascus, in Ash-Sham(ألشام).

129
00:12:43,067 --> 00:12:49,150
By the way, you might have heard of this story of Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب),

130
00:12:49,554 --> 00:12:54,270
removing Khalid Ibn Walid(خالد ابن وليد) from his post, as the leader of the armies.

131
00:12:54,981 --> 00:12:57,632
And there's a lot of fabricated stories that surround that,

132
00:12:57,826 --> 00:13:01,702
that there was a personal jealousy between them and they didn't like each other

133
00:13:01,849 --> 00:13:03,857
and they had to fight when they're young.

134
00:13:04,188 --> 00:13:08,314
So, they kept this grudge against each other when they grew old - nonsense.

135
00:13:08,759 --> 00:13:13,714
The reason why Khalid Ibn Walid(خالد ابن وليد) was removed from his post

136
00:13:14,205 --> 00:13:22,120
was because Umar Bin Khattab رضي الله عنه his method of governance was different than Abu Bakr(ابوبكر).

137
00:13:22,426 --> 00:13:27,128
Abu Bakr(ابوبكر), he gave a lot of independence to his governors.

138
00:13:27,577 --> 00:13:33,034
So, financially every governor was independent from the capital of Khilafah(خِلَافَه).

139
00:13:34,007 --> 00:13:40,585
So, every governor has independence and how they would collect money and how they would spend it,

140
00:13:41,030 --> 00:13:43,202
 that was the way in the time of Abu Bakr(ابوبكر).

141
00:13:43,499 --> 00:13:49,313
However, with Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) he wanted the financial issues to be centralized.

142
00:13:49,851 --> 00:13:55,123
So, he wanted every governor, every military general to submit

143
00:13:56,650 --> 00:14:00,294
an account of where did he make the money and how did he spend it.?

144
00:14:01,033 --> 00:14:05,166
So, he told Khalid Ibn Walid(خالد ابن وليد), I want from you reports

145
00:14:05,416 --> 00:14:10,371
on how you collect your money, the Ghanaem(غنائم), the Nafel(نفل) everything

146
00:14:10,614 --> 00:14:12,026
and how you spend it,

147
00:14:12,581 --> 00:14:16,787
Khalid Bin Waleed رضي الله عنه, did not like that, and he wasn't happy with that method.

148
00:14:16,827 --> 00:14:21,756
 He said: In the time of Abu Bakr(ابوبكر), I had a dependence to collect the money and spend it the way I see fit.

149
00:14:22,115 --> 00:14:24,151
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) said: Well, that's not my way.

150
00:14:24,553 --> 00:14:27,521
My way is that I will hold you accountable for every penny.

151
00:14:28,303 --> 00:14:30,694
Khalid Ibn Walid(خالد ابن وليد) said: than I don't want to work for you.

152
00:14:30,901 --> 00:14:35,415
And that is when he resigned and he was removed by Umar Ibn Al-Khattab رضي الله عنه.

153
00:14:35,440 --> 00:14:36,890
That was the first removal.

154
00:14:38,144 --> 00:14:45,039
However, in another battle, when Khalid Ibn Walid(خالد ابن وليد) was under Abu Obaidah(ابوعبيدة).

155
00:14:46,029 --> 00:14:50,742
Abu Obaidah(ابوعبيدة) sent an army to open a particular town

156
00:14:51,678 --> 00:14:54,215
and Khalid Ibn Walid(خالد ابن وليد) was with that army.

157
00:14:55,695 --> 00:15:00,480
Events happened in a way where the leadership was killed.

158
00:15:00,504 --> 00:15:02,990
So, Khalid Ibn Walid(خالد ابن وليد) took over leadership,

159
00:15:04,239 --> 00:15:08,020
he took over leadership not because of love of leadership, but because he had to,

160
00:15:08,200 --> 00:15:09,467
there was nobody around to do it.

161
00:15:09,560 --> 00:15:13,188
So, he came forth and he assumed leadership

162
00:15:13,348 --> 00:15:16,904
and then he became the governor of this new place.

163
00:15:17,421 --> 00:15:20,207
When news reached Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) he said;

164
00:15:20,437 --> 00:15:26,420
خالد إبن وليد أَمَّارَهْ نَفْسَه، لَقَدْ كَانَ أبوبكر أَعْلَمْ بِرِّجَالِ مِنِّيْ

165
00:15:26,962 --> 00:15:32,987
He said: It is Khalid(خالد), who appointed himself as Ameer(أمير),

166
00:15:33,752 --> 00:15:38,126
and may Allah have mercy on Abu Bakr(ابوبكر), he knew the men better than me.

167
00:15:38,699 --> 00:15:44,098
This was a man that was so capable that in this situation of difficulty,

168
00:15:44,316 --> 00:15:50,063
he rise to the occasion and he became the leader and he saved the Muslims at that particular day.

169
00:15:50,334 --> 00:15:53,918
And Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) was saying that Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) knows the men better than I do.

170
00:15:55,157 --> 00:15:59,110
However, they had another dispute on financial issues.

171
00:15:59,135 --> 00:16:01,082
So, he had to remove Khalid Ibn Walid(خالد ابن وليد) again.

172
00:16:02,423 --> 00:16:04,864
And this time, there was another reason.

173
00:16:05,710 --> 00:16:09,062
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) said: I want the people to know

174
00:16:09,087 --> 00:16:12,560
that I didn't remove Khalid Ibn Walid(خالد ابن وليد) because I dislike him

175
00:16:12,804 --> 00:16:14,556
or I'm not happy with his conduct.

176
00:16:15,211 --> 00:16:17,211
The reason, why I removed him?

177
00:16:17,343 --> 00:16:21,268
Is because I wanted people to know that it is Allah, Who gives victory.

178
00:16:23,589 --> 00:16:27,975
Because Khalid Ibn Walid(خالد ابن وليد) never, ever lost a battle in his life

179
00:16:29,033 --> 00:16:33,547
in Islam or before Islam, he was becoming a legend

180
00:16:36,064 --> 00:16:38,170
and he was becoming a Fitnah(فِتْنَه) for people,

181
00:16:38,837 --> 00:16:42,941
people start thinking that as long as Khalid(خالد) is leading you cannot lose.

182
00:16:44,025 --> 00:16:48,006
So, Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) did not want that flaw to enter in the hearts of men

183
00:16:48,031 --> 00:16:51,840
and start depending on the creation rather than depending on Allah.

184
00:16:51,865 --> 00:16:53,384
He said: I wanted people to know

185
00:16:53,580 --> 00:16:56,942
 that victory doesn't really come from Khalid Ibn Walid(خالدابن وليد), it comes from Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ.

186
00:16:57,762 --> 00:17:00,608
So, he was protecting the Aqeedah(عقيدة) of the people protecting their Eeman(ايمان)

187
00:17:00,632 --> 00:17:03,110
