771
01:04:56,380 --> 01:05:01,857
in Qur'an it says that if a Muslim is facing twice their size,

772
01:05:01,882 --> 01:05:07,697
if a Muslim army is facing more than twice the size then they're allowed to retreat

773
01:05:08,193 --> 01:05:14,840
However, this scholar say: If the Muslim army is over 12,000, no matter how large the enemy is,

774
01:05:15,433 --> 01:05:16,998
they're not allowed to retreat.

775
01:05:18,448 --> 01:05:19,815
Even if you're facing a million

776
01:05:21,848 --> 01:05:25,787
that rule only applies to armies less than 12,000, that's according to some scholars,

777
01:05:26,877 --> 01:05:27,568
it's one view.

778
01:05:29,546 --> 01:05:32,826
Amr Bin Al-Aas(عَمْرُو بِن اَلْعَاص) counts he only has 4000 soldiers,

779
01:05:34,636 --> 01:05:36,776
where are the 12,000?

780
01:05:40,948 --> 01:05:50,250
He actually had more because Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) sent him in the letter saying;

781
01:05:51,099 --> 01:05:54,505
 I sent you 4000 soldiers

782
01:05:56,457 --> 01:06:01,612
each thousand is headed by a man who is equal to 1000.

783
01:06:04,433 --> 01:06:08,771
I've sent you Az-Zubair Bin Awwam(ألزبير بن عوام), Al-Miqdad Ibn Amr(ألمقدادإبن عمرو),

784
01:06:09,358 --> 01:06:12,290
Maslimma Bin Makhlad(مسلمةبن مخلد) and Ubadah Bin Samit(عبادة بن الصامت).

785
01:06:12,990 --> 01:06:15,461
Each one of these men is equal to 1000.

786
01:06:15,596 --> 01:06:17,818
Therefore, you have 12,000.

787
01:06:19,401 --> 01:06:23,428
That's the calculation of Umar(عُمَر), Amr Bin Al-Aas(عَمْرُو بِن اَلْعَاص) is counting how many as 4000

788
01:06:23,823 --> 01:06:30,274
but now he has to change the figure to 12,000 because of these four men.

789
01:06:31,646 --> 01:06:35,079
Again Az-Zubair Bin Awwam(ألزبير بن عوام), Al-Miqdad Ibn Amr(ألمقدادإبن عمرو),

790
01:06:37,036 --> 01:06:39,584
Maslimma Bin Makhlad(مسلمةبن مخلد) and Ubadah Bin Samit(عبادة بن الصامت),

791
01:06:42,078 --> 01:06:44,555
they opened that fortress, how did they open it?

792
01:06:45,148 --> 01:06:48,393
You can see that really one man, can he be equal to 1000?

793
01:06:49,929 --> 01:06:54,031
Az-Zubair Bin Awwam(ألزبير بن عوام), who's leading 1000 men

794
01:06:54,749 --> 01:07:00,924
advances against this fortress, he asks his men to prepare a ladder for him to climb,

795
01:07:01,229 --> 01:07:05,009
he climbs on the highest tower of the fortress alone

796
01:07:05,847 --> 01:07:08,913
and he raises up his sword and he makes Takbeer(تكبير),

797
01:07:10,521 --> 01:07:14,485
when the enemy saw that they thought that the Muslims already broke in

798
01:07:14,857 --> 01:07:16,836
because how could he be standing on that tower

799
01:07:17,669 --> 01:07:21,569
and if he's standing alone, he must be surrounded by Guards from every direction.

800
01:07:22,228 --> 01:07:24,332
So, they immediately gave up, that was it.

801
01:07:24,815 --> 01:07:29,574
One man opened this fortress.

802
01:07:31,435 --> 01:07:34,111
This was Az-Zubair Bin Awwam(ألزبير بن عوام), you know there's a story they say that

803
01:07:35,092 --> 01:07:44,315
once he struck one of the enemy soldiers on his shoulder, this enemy soldier was on his horse,

804
01:07:46,396 --> 01:07:50,922
his sword went through until, the man fell from both sides

805
01:07:52,195 --> 01:07:57,365
and it went down a bit further and cut the saddle, the saddle of the horse.

806
01:07:57,907 --> 01:07:59,019
So, the saddle fell.

807
01:08:01,440 --> 01:08:06,368
So the Sahabah(صحابه) said: Allah Ho Akbar(الله أكبر) your sword is powerful.

808
01:08:06,735 --> 01:08:12,332
He said: It's not the sword, it's my arm, don't give credit to the sword, it's my arm.

809
01:08:17,551 --> 01:08:24,496
But it took them seven months to open that fortress.

810
01:08:30,156 --> 01:08:36,033
And now, they move on to the most important town in Egypt and that's Alexandria.

811
01:08:36,436 --> 01:08:38,137
Cairo didn't exist yet.

812
01:08:38,265 --> 01:08:40,292
Cairo was rebuilt later by the Muslims.

813
01:08:40,749 --> 01:08:42,477
The major town was Alexandria.

814
01:08:42,963 --> 01:08:46,763
So, they lay siege to Alexandria,

815
01:08:47,464 --> 01:08:53,718
and it was taking some time, and Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) was losing patience.

816
01:08:55,521 --> 01:08:58,431
So, he sends a letter to Amr Bin Al-Aas(عَمْرُو بِن اَلْعَاص), he said;

817
01:08:58,849 --> 01:09:02,829
أَمَّا بَعْدَ، فَقَدْ عَجِبْتُ لِإِبْطَائِكُمْ عَنْ فَتْحِ مصر

818
01:09:03,279 --> 01:09:06,203
إِنَّكُمْ تُقَاتِلُوْنَهُمْ مُنْذُ سَنَتَيْنَ

819
01:09:06,805 --> 01:09:12,993
مَا ذَلِكَ إِلَّا لِمَا أَحْدَثْتُمْ، وَأَحْبَبْتُمْ مِنَّ الدُنْيَا مَا أَحَبَّ عَدُوَّكُمْ

820
01:09:13,586 --> 01:09:18,543
He said: I am surprised because of the slow action in Egypt.

821
01:09:18,903 --> 01:09:22,680
You've been fighting them for two years and you didn't open it yet.

822
01:09:23,278 --> 01:09:25,483
That must be because of your sins.

823
01:09:25,700 --> 01:09:28,731
And because you are now loving Duniyah(دُنِيَّا) just like your enemy.

824
01:09:30,189 --> 01:09:32,086
He said: How come it's taking two years?

825
01:09:32,927 --> 01:09:34,367
Why is it so slow?

826
01:09:34,774 --> 01:09:38,435
It's because you are loving Duniyah(دُنِيَّا) just like your enemy and then he said;

827
01:09:39,618 --> 01:09:43,015
وَإِنَّ الله تَبَارَكَ وَتَعَالى لَا يَنْصُرُ قَوْمًاإِلَّابِصِدْقٍ نِّيَّاتِهِمْ،

828
01:09:43,363 --> 01:09:46,637
And Allah will never give you victory, except if you have pure intentions.

829
01:09:47,504 --> 01:09:59,119
وَقَدْ كُنْتُ وَجَّهْتَ إِلَيْكَ أَرْبَعَةُ نَفَرٍ وَأَعْلَمْتُكَ أَنَّ الرَّجُلَ مِنْهُمْ مَقَامَ أَلْفِ رَجُلٍ

830
01:09:59,498 --> 01:10:03,888
عَلى مَا كُنْتُ أَعْرِفْ،إِلَّاأَنْ يَّكُوْنَ غَيَّرَ هُمْ مَا غَيَّرَ غَيْرَهُمْ

831
01:10:04,645 --> 01:10:09,911
And I have sent you for men each man as equal to 1000 according to my knowledge,

832
01:10:10,239 --> 01:10:13,197
except if they have changed like the rest of you.

833
01:10:16,007 --> 01:10:19,242
فَإِذَا أَتَاكَ كِتَابِيْ هَذَا فَاخْطُبِ النَّاسْ

834
01:10:19,995 --> 01:10:23,928
وَحُضَّهُمْ عَلى قِتَالِ عَدُّوِّهِمْ وَرَغِّبْهُمْ فِيْ الصَّبْرِ وَالنِّيَهْ

835
01:10:24,101 --> 01:10:26,579
وَقَدِّمْ أُوْلَئِكَ الأَرْبَعَةْفِيْ صُدُوْرِ النَّاسْ

836
01:10:26,912 --> 01:10:30,856
 When you receive this letter of mine, stand up and give a speech your people

837
01:10:31,075 --> 01:10:33,686
and encourage them to the to fight in the path of Allah

838
01:10:33,872 --> 01:10:35,604
and encourage them to have patience

839
01:10:35,810 --> 01:10:41,179
and good intentions and make those four men ahead of everybody else.

840
01:10:42,039 --> 01:10:45,824
وَمُرِ النَّاسَ جَمِيْعًا أَنْ يَكُوْنَ لَهُمْ صَدْمَةْ كَصَدْمَةْ رَجُلْ وَاحِدْ،

841
01:10:46,539 --> 01:10:50,501
And order your army to attack like one man, all at once.

842
01:10:51,676 --> 01:10:57,782
وَلْيَكُنْ ذَلِكَ عِنْدَ الزَّوَّالْ يَوْمَ الْجُمْعَةْ، فَإِنَّهَا سَاعَةٌ تَنَزَّلُ فِيْهَا الرَّحْمَةْ

843
01:10:58,035 --> 01:11:02,065
وَوَقْتُ الْإِجَابَةْ،وَلِيُعَجَّ النَّاسْ إِلَى الله وَيَسْأَلُوْهُ النَّصْرَ عَلَى عَدُوِّهِمْ

844
01:11:02,405 --> 01:11:06,450
And let that attack be in the time of Salaat-Ul-Jumu'ah(صلاة الجمعة)

845
01:11:07,475 --> 01:11:11,458
because that is a time, when Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ accepts the Dua(دُعَا)

846
01:11:11,727 --> 01:11:14,857
and you should all be making Dua(دُعَا) to Allah to give you victory.

847
01:11:16,586 --> 01:11:18,392
You should do it in the time of Khutba-Jumu'ah(خطبة الجمعة)

848
01:11:18,417 --> 01:11:20,560
when the people are praying and making Dua(دُعَا) for you.

849
01:11:23,869 --> 01:11:30,012
Alexandria was opened, and Amr Bin Al-Aas(عَمْرُو بِن اَلْعَاص) immediately,

850
01:11:31,363 --> 01:11:33,688
dispatches Muawiya Bin Hadeej(معاوية بن حديج)

851
01:11:33,782 --> 01:11:36,505
to go to Madina to deliver the good news to Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب).

852
01:11:38,711 --> 01:11:45,493
Muawiya Bin Hadeej(معاوية بن حديج) arrives into Madina at the time of Zuhar(الظهر) .

853
01:11:45,959 --> 01:11:49,727
Now I've narrated it to you, I think the story before and I attributed it to

854
01:11:49,817 --> 01:11:52,992
Abu Muslim Al-Khaulani(أبومسلم ألخولاني), sometimes you would have narrations

855
01:11:53,242 --> 01:11:56,687
and an attribute to different people, this story is a bit different.

856
01:11:56,712 --> 01:11:59,066
It might be the same story or it might be a separate one.

857
01:11:59,561 --> 01:12:02,380
Muawiya Bin Hadeej(معاوية بن حديج) arrives into Madina at noon.

858
01:12:02,671 --> 01:12:03,863
So, he goes to the Masjid(مسجد)

859
01:12:04,084 --> 01:12:06,110
because he thought that the Khalifah(خليفه) is asleep,

860
01:12:07,171 --> 01:12:09,795
in the time of noon, siesta, everybody sleeps in Madina.

861
01:12:09,820 --> 01:12:14,218
There's nothing could do it, it's too hot, no Air Conditions, so you stay indoors,

862
01:12:18,409 --> 01:12:20,927
Muawiya Bin Hadeej(معاوية بن حديج) he gets to the Masjid(مسجد)

863
01:12:20,952 --> 01:12:22,775
and he talks to the people about the good news.

864
01:12:24,683 --> 01:12:27,812
And he was walking in the street, so a slave girl saw him.

865
01:12:28,746 --> 01:12:31,612
She belongs to Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب), she saw his clothes,

866
01:12:31,637 --> 01:12:34,232
and she realized that this is a man who just came back from travel.

867
01:12:34,297 --> 01:12:36,052
So, she went to Umar(عُمَر) and she said,

868
01:12:36,387 --> 01:12:39,447
that there's a man outside and just came back from travel.

869
01:12:39,554 --> 01:12:40,682
He said: Bring him in.

870
01:12:41,586 --> 01:12:44,932
So, she called him and Muawiya Bin Hadeej(معاوية بن حديج) entered.

871
01:12:45,382 --> 01:12:46,887
And Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) told him;

872
01:12:47,028 --> 01:12:47,961
 "ما ورآعك"

873
01:12:48,524 --> 01:12:49,803
What news do you have?

874
01:12:50,199 --> 01:12:55,519
He said: I have good news, Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ gave us victory and we opened Alexandria,

875
01:12:56,528 --> 01:12:58,233
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) said: Come with me.

876
01:12:59,078 --> 01:13:00,524
He took me to the Masjid(مسجد). He said;

877
01:13:00,558 --> 01:13:01,366
"ألصّلاة الجامع"

878
01:13:01,390 --> 01:13:03,584
He invited all of the people to come to the Masjid(مسجد).

879
01:13:03,940 --> 01:13:06,804
And then he had Muawiya(معاويه) deliver the good news.

880
01:13:07,718 --> 01:13:10,441
And then he takes Muawiya(معاويه) back with him to his house.

881
01:13:10,890 --> 01:13:13,778
Muawiya(معاويه) said: Umar(عُمَر) entered the house, he faced Qibla(قبله).

882
01:13:13,905 --> 01:13:16,680
And he started making Dua(دُعَا) thanking Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ.

883
01:13:17,798 --> 01:13:21,010
And then he said: You are a traveler, you are in need of eating.

884
01:13:21,441 --> 01:13:24,108
So, he bought me bread and oil.

885
01:13:25,032 --> 01:13:28,559
So, I was dipping their bread and oil and eating it, I didn't have much because I was shy,

886
01:13:28,978 --> 01:13:31,962
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) be told me to eat because you are a traveler.

887
01:13:33,198 --> 01:13:37,301
When I finished my meal. He said: Muawiya(معاويه)! What did you do in the Masjid(مسجد)?

888
01:13:39,549 --> 01:13:42,072
He said: Well, I told the people about what happened.?

889
01:13:42,096 --> 01:13:43,776
He said: Why didn't you come to me first?

890
01:13:43,832 --> 01:13:47,545
You know, it's inappropriate to go and talk to the people before you talk to the Ameer(أمير).

891
01:13:48,264 --> 01:13:50,181
The news needs to be delivered to Ameer(أمير).

892
01:13:50,991 --> 01:13:52,734
He said: I thought that you were asleep.

893
01:13:54,199 --> 01:13:56,266
He said: Woe to you. How can I sleep?

894
01:13:56,720 --> 01:14:01,704
If I sleep during the day, I would not fulfill my responsibilities towards my people.

895
01:14:02,259 --> 01:14:08,454
And if I sleep at night, I would not be fulfilling my duties towards Allah, when can I sleep.?

896
01:14:09,071 --> 01:14:10,534
أَيْحَاتَ، أَيْحَاتَ أَنَا نَعَمْ

897
01:14:11,283 --> 01:14:13,270
 He was cutting his sleeping time short

898
01:14:13,814 --> 01:14:19,076
because he wanted to fulfill his duties towards Allah and towards his people.

899
01:14:19,389 --> 01:14:24,358
Ask yourself the question, how many moments or hours or days or months

900
01:14:24,600 --> 01:14:27,745
or years are you wasting from your valuable time.

901
01:14:28,522 --> 01:14:30,895
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) didn't even have time to sleep?

902
01:14:31,676 --> 01:14:35,419
Do not waste your time because there's so much that needs to be done.

903
01:14:35,637 --> 01:14:37,946
أَلْوَاجِبَاتُ أَكْثَرْ مِنْ أَوْقَاتْ

904
01:14:38,193 --> 01:14:41,568
 The duties are more than our time.

905
01:14:48,861 --> 01:14:52,710
Amr Bin Al-Aas(عَمْرُو بِن اَلْعَاص) sends a letter to Umar(عُمَر) giving him some other good news.

906
01:14:53,178 --> 01:14:56,994
He said: O Umar(عمر), we've built for you a house in Egypt

907
01:14:58,428 --> 01:15:01,370
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) sent him back a letter, he said;

908
01:15:02,030 --> 01:15:05,189
What would the man living in Hijaaz(حجاز) do with a house in Egypt?

909
01:15:07,935 --> 01:15:11,450
Turn it into a marketplace for Muslims, turn it into shops?

910
01:15:11,778 --> 01:15:13,471
Why are you building a house for me in Egypt?

911
01:15:14,662 --> 01:15:21,505
I'm not like other kings or emperors who have a palace, in each and every town, give it to the Muslims.

912
01:15:24,022 --> 01:15:28,803
Finally, the last thing

913
01:15:29,769 --> 01:15:35,586
Amr Bin Al-Aas(عَمْرُو بِن اَلْعَاص), now the head of the army in Egypt was appointed as governor of Egypt

914
01:15:35,923 --> 01:15:38,669
and he would remain the governor of Egypt until the end of his life.

915
01:15:39,603 --> 01:15:48,332
But Egypt is a land of blessings, it's very fertile land and it's wealthy, it's rich.

916
01:15:48,356 --> 01:15:53,129
The Romans were using it as a milking cow not to feed its people but to feed them.

917
01:15:54,571 --> 01:15:56,492
Amr Bin Al-Aas(عَمْرُو بِن اَلْعَاص) is aware of this

918
01:15:56,953 --> 01:16:01,011
and he is coming in with people from the Arabian Peninsula from the desert

919
01:16:03,351 --> 01:16:08,569
and the food in Egypt can make you fat, you'd gain weight,

920
01:16:11,212 --> 01:16:14,892
unlike what the Arabs were brought up within Hijaaz(حجاز) or in Najd(نجد).

921
01:16:18,750 --> 01:16:23,067
So, Amr Bin Al-Aas(عَمْرُو بِن اَلْعَاص) told his soldiers;

922
01:16:24,055 --> 01:16:28,145
وَلَا أَعْلَمَنَّا مَا أَتَا رَجُلْ قَدْ أَسْمَنَ جِسْمَه’ وَأَهْذَلَ فَرَسَ

923
01:16:28,856 --> 01:16:32,312
I do not want to see any of you gaining weight

924
01:16:33,106 --> 01:16:35,439
while your horse is losing weight.

925
01:16:37,564 --> 01:16:38,246
And then he said;

926
01:16:39,272 --> 01:16:44,793
وَعْلَمُوْ أَنِّيْ مُعْرِزُوْنَلْ خَيْلَ كَعَاتِرَاذِلرِّجَاْل

927
01:16:45,094 --> 01:16:49,381
فَمَنْ أَهْزَلَ فَرَسَه’ مِنْ غَيْرِ عِلَّهْ حَطَّتُ مِنْ فَرِيْضَتَه’ قَدَرَ ذَلِكْ

928
01:16:49,858 --> 01:16:52,335
And I'm going to have your parade in front of me,

929
01:16:52,545 --> 01:16:55,081
and I'm going to have your horses parade in front of me.

930
01:16:55,788 --> 01:17:02,602
And if I see any of your horses losing weight, you will have your salary cut.

931
01:17:05,203 --> 01:17:10,397
We are soldiers Fee-Sabeel-Lillah(فِي سَبيل الله) our life, is a life of a soldier,

932
01:17:11,315 --> 01:17:15,619
a military lifestyle, that is who we are! And that is who we will be!

933
01:17:16,057 --> 01:17:18,222
And we will remain following this tough regimen.

934
01:17:20,044 --> 01:17:25,789
If I see you gaining weight in Egypt and if I see your horses being neglected.

935
01:17:28,590 --> 01:17:31,616
I will reduce your salaries, your salaries will be cut.

936
01:17:32,460 --> 01:17:37,560
So, stay fit and take care of your horses.

937
01:17:38,269 --> 01:17:43,047
This was the Ibadah(عبادة) this was the understanding of the Sahabah(صحابه) in Islam.

938
01:17:43,939 --> 01:17:46,658
It was not just, you do your Salah(صلاة)

939
01:17:46,924 --> 01:17:53,807
and grow a big belly and grow a big beard and that's it, you're an excellent Muslim.

940
01:17:56,614 --> 01:17:59,863
He said: You will be paraded in front of me you on your horses

941
01:18:00,145 --> 01:18:03,300
and I'm going to hold you accountable and see how fit you are.

942
01:18:04,856 --> 01:18:07,438
This is how Sahabah رضي الله عنه lived their lives.

943
01:18:09,187 --> 01:18:12,311
 One of the Sahabah(صحابه) at old age he was so old

944
01:18:14,046 --> 01:18:18,849
and he would still run between the targets when he is practicing archery.

945
01:18:19,783 --> 01:18:23,112
They told him: Why don't you stop, your are old in age.

946
01:18:23,408 --> 01:18:31,328
He said: I'm running in a garden in paradise.

947
01:18:31,918 --> 01:18:34,298
that was Ibadah(عبادة) for them, he was worshipping Allah.

948
01:18:35,160 --> 01:18:40,990
In fact, in another Hadith(حديث) it says that while the Sahabah(صحابه) were practicing in Madina, target shooting.

949
01:18:41,256 --> 01:18:46,712
It was time for Salah(صلاة), so Rasool Allah ﷺ said: They are in a Salah(صلاة).

950
01:18:49,056 --> 01:18:53,831
So, that was the life of the Sahabah رضي الله عنهم that was the ideal and perfect way of living.

951
01:18:54,261 --> 01:18:56,620
We ask Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ to guide us to the truth.

952
01:18:58,347 --> 01:19:00,847
We're almost done with the Ghazawat(غزوات), pretty much done.

953
01:19:00,872 --> 01:19:03,594
We just have a few bits and pieces miscellaneous stuff left

954
01:19:04,253 --> 01:19:06,396
that will take maybe half a session or one session

955
01:19:06,535 --> 01:19:11,192
and then we'll be talking about the last moments in the life of a Umar Bin Khattab رضي الله عنه.

956
01:19:11,481 --> 01:19:15,529
IT SHUDDERS IN PAIN FREELY

957
01:19:15,654 --> 01:19:19,843
MY CHASITY, MY MODESTY!

958
01:19:19,962 --> 01:19:23,838
OH MUSLIM, YOU SAW

959
01:19:24,236 --> 01:19:28,372
MY INJURY AND THE INJURY OF MY PRIDE

